questions.stem:
A garage tests horns with this fragment:
class Horn { String sound() { return "beep"; } }
class TruckHorn extends Horn { String sound() { return "HONK"; } }
Horn h = new TruckHorn();
System.out.print(h.sound() + new Horn().sound());
What is printed?

A print shop labels posters with this fragment:
class Poster { String label = "base"; }
class Glossy extends Poster { String label = "kid"; }
Poster x = new Glossy();
System.out.println(x.label);
What is printed?

A registry classifies units with this fragment:
class Unit { static String kind() { return "U"; } }
class Squad extends Unit { static String kind() { return "S"; } }
Unit x = new Squad();
System.out.println(x.kind());
What is printed?

A gallery totals floor space polymorphically with this helper:
public static int totalArea(Shape[] gallery) {
  int t = 0;
  for (Shape s : gallery) t += _____;
  return t;
}
Which expression belongs in the blank?

A depot expects BEEP from this code but hears beep:
class Alarm { public String sound() { return "beep"; } }
class CarAlarm extends Alarm { public String sound(int n) { return "BEEP"; } }
Alarm a = new CarAlarm();
System.out.println(a.sound());
What is the fault?

A mural app measures walls with this fragment:
class Mural { int area() { return 5; } }
class BigMural extends Mural { int area() { return 7; } }
Mural m = new BigMural();
System.out.println(m.area() + new Mural().area());
What integer is printed?

A depot prints routes only for ferries with this fragment:
class Vessel { }
class Ferry extends Vessel { int routes() { return 6; } }
Vessel v = new Ferry();
if (v instanceof Ferry) System.out.println(((Ferry) v).routes());
What integer is printed?

A harbor desk crashes when docking a plain vessel here:
public static void dock(Vessel v) { Ferry f = (Ferry) v; System.out.println(f.routes()); }
The call dock(new Vessel()) throws. What is the fault?

A fare helper counts ferry routes from any vessel:
public static int ferryRoutes(Vessel v) {
  if (_____) { return ((Ferry) v).routes(); }
  return 0;
}
Which test belongs in the blank?

A lost-and-found box holds this fragment:
Object o = Integer.valueOf(7);
String s = (String) o;
What happens when it runs?

A dockmaster counts ferries in this lineup:
Vessel[] dock = {new Ferry(3), new Vessel(), new Ferry(5), new Vessel()};
int n = 0;
for (Vessel v : dock) { if (v instanceof Ferry) n++; }
System.out.println(n);
Here Ferry(int r) stores a route count. What integer is printed?

A gate prices one vessel with this fragment:
Vessel v = new Ferry(4);
if (v instanceof Ferry f) System.out.println(f.routes());
Here Ferry(int r) stores a route count. What integer is printed?

A gate handles a missing vessel with this fragment:
Vessel v = null;
if (v instanceof Ferry f) System.out.println(f.routes());
else System.out.println(-1);
What integer is printed?

A turnstile program fails to compile here:
if (v instanceof Ferry f) { System.out.println("ok"); }
System.out.println(f.routes());
What is the fault?

A dispatcher prints ferry routes without any cast:
if (_____) { System.out.println(f.routes()); }
Which test belongs in the blank?

A gate labels ferries with this fragment:
Vessel v = new Ferry(1);
if (v instanceof Ferry f && f.routes() > 2) System.out.println("express");
else System.out.println("local");
What is printed?

A lobby kiosk greets guests through this fragment:
interface Greeter { default String greet() { return "welcome"; } }
class Host implements Greeter { }
System.out.println(new Host().greet());
What is printed?

A badge printer fails to compile here:
interface A { default String tag() { return "a"; } }
interface B { default String tag() { return "b"; } }
class C implements A, B { }
What is the fault?

A logging contract ships a ready-made header:
interface Log { _____ String head() { return "log:"; } }
Which keyword belongs in the blank?

A swim final orders finalists by seconds with this class:
class Swimmer implements Comparable<Swimmer> {
  String name; int secs;
  public int compareTo(Swimmer o) { return this.secs - o.secs; }
}
Finalists hold Ana 52, Ben 48, Cid 55. After sorting with compareTo, whose name prints first?

A leaderboard shows the slowest runner first because of this method:
public int compareTo(Runner o) { return o.time - this.time; }
What is the fault?
